          "status": "canonical",
          "op": "replace",
          "note": "The style's signature move on its most ambitious houses: boards bevelled, laid flush, scored to imitate ashlar coursing, and painted with sand thrown into the wet paint so the surface takes the light like cut stone -- the Isaac Royall House and the Jeremiah Lee Mansion both do this."
